r-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335462" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\text{L1 and L3}"] ["math" "\\text{L3 and L4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335462" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\text{L3 and L4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335462" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335462" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "the absorption property"] ["text" "the constant multiple property"] ["text" "the reflexive property"] ["text" "the sum property"] ["text" "the transitive property"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335462" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "the transitive property"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335445" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)=2+{e}^{-x},$ then $f=O(1)$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,f=O(2+{e}^{-x})$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{2}=0$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,{e}^{-x}=O(2)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,f=O(2)$  \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O(1)$  \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from lines  \n{{field-2}}  \nand  \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line  \n{{field-4}}  \nand  \n{{field-5}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335445" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation. \n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property. \n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen \n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\nf=O({{2+{e}^{-x}}_{⏟}}_{f}),\n$$\n\nand this is true by the $\\text{reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ From line $\\text{L1}$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(2+{e}^{-x}),\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\n{e}^{-x}=O(2).\n$$\n\nThus, by lines   $\\text{L1 and L3}$ and the  $\\text{absorption property},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf=O(2).\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line $\\text{L4},$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(2)\n$$\n\nand by the $\\text{constant multiple property}$ with $c=2,$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(1).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335445" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "389bad3a918409e6507ef083a82b655a9c08328ee3cf37bb2dc83d698fc5818e"} {"question" "q-335445" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335445" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "the absorption property"] ["text" "the constant multiple property"] ["text" "the reflexive property"] ["text" "the sum property"] ["text" "the transitive property"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335445" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "the reflexive property"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335445" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335445" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\text{L1 and L3}"] ["math" "\\text{L2 and L3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335445" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\text{L1 and L3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335445" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335445" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "the absorption property"] ["text" "the constant multiple property"] ["text" "the reflexive property"] ["text" "the sum property"] ["text" "the transitive property"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335445" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "the absorption property"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335445" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335445" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\text{L2}"] ["math" "\\text{L3}"] ["math" "\\text{L4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335445" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\text{L4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335445" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335445" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "the absorption property"] ["text" "the constant multiple property"] ["text" "the reflexive property"] ["text" "the sum property"] ["text" "the transitive property"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335445" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "the constant multiple property"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)=2{e}^{4x}+x,$ then $f=O({e}^{4x})$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,2{e}^{4x}=O(2{e}^{4x})$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{x}{2{e}^{4x}})=0$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,x=O(2{e}^{4x})$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,f=O(4{e}^{4x})$  \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O({e}^{4x})$  \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from lines  \n{{field-2}}  \nand  \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line  \n{{field-4}}  \nand  \n{{field-5}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation.\n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property.\n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let us justify each selected step.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\n2{e}^{4x}=O(2{e}^{4x}),\n$$\n\nand this follows by $\\text{the reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ From line $\\text{L1}$ we have\n\n$$\n2{e}^{4x}=O(2{e}^{4x}),\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nx=O(2{e}^{4x}).\n$$\n\nSince $f=2{e}^{4x}+x,$ by lines $\\text{L1 and L3}$ and $\\text{the sum property},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf=2{e}^{4x}+x=O(2{e}^{4x}+2{e}^{4x})=O(4{e}^{4x}),\n$$\n\nwhich justifies line $\\text{L4}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line $\\text{L4}$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(4{e}^{4x}),\n$$\n\nand by $\\text{the constant multiple property}$ with $c=4,$ we conclude\n\n$$\nf=O({e}^{4x}).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "389bad3a918409e6507ef083a82b655a9c08328ee3cf37bb2dc83d698fc5818e"} {"question" "q-335071" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335071" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "the absorption property"] ["text" "the constant multiple property"] ["text" "the reflexive property"] ["text" "the sum property"] ["text" "the transitive property"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335071" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "the reflexive property"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335071" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335071" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$"] ["text" "$\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335071" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335071" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335071" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "the absorption property"] ["text" "the constant multiple property"] ["text" "the reflexive property"] ["text" "the sum property"] ["text" "the transitive property"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335071" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "the sum property"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335071" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335071" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\text{L2}"] ["math" "\\text{L3}"] ["math" "\\text{L4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335071" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\text{L4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335071" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335071" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "the absorption property"] ["text" "the constant multiple property"] ["text" "the reflexive property"] ["text" "the sum property"] ["text" "the transitive property"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335071" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "the constant multiple property"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)=3x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,$ then $f=O(x)$ as $x\\to 0.$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,3x=O(3x)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,{lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{2x})=1$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=O(2x)$ as $x\\to 0$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,f=O(5x)$ as $x\\to 0$ \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O(x)$ as $x\\to 0$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from lines \n{{field-2}} and \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line {{field-4}}  and \n{{field-5}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation. \n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property.\n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let us justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\n3x=O({{3x}_{⏟}}_{f}).\n$$\n\nThis is true by $\\text{the reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ From line $\\text{L1}$ we have\n\n$$\n3x=O(3x),\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\n-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=O(2x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\nThus, by lines $\\text{L1 and L3}$ and $\\text{the sum property},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf=O(5x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line  $\\text{L4}$   we have\n\n$$\nf=O(5x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0,\n$$\n\nand by the $\\text{constant multiple property}$ with $c=5,$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "389bad3a918409e6507ef083a82b655a9c08328ee3cf37bb2dc83d698fc5818e"} {"question" "q-335438" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "b0034e82136d0f96f12cbd0f2af21b53d51a3833967616675e55a323ea02e503"} {"question" "q-335438" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "the absorption property"] ["text" "the constant multiple property"] ["text" "the reflexive property"] ["text" "the sum property"] ["text" "the transitive property"]] "